  "start_command": "npm --prefix '../../../output/tournament-baseline-full' run dev",
  "summary": "A single-user tabletop tournament manager: set name and date, add/edit/remove players (no duplicates, min 3), auto-generate a round-robin schedule with byes for odd counts, enter and correct scores with draws, filter matches by round/player/status, track progress, and view live standings (win=3, draw=1, tiebreak by difference then points scored then alphabetical). All data persists in localStorage and survives refresh.",
  "implemented_features": [
    "Name and date the tournament",
    "Add players with duplicate detection (case-insensitive) and empty-name validation",
    "Edit and remove players before the schedule is made",
    "Minimum of 3 players required to make the schedule",
    "Round-robin schedule: every pair plays once, no player twice in a round, byes for odd player counts",
    "Player list is locked once the schedule is made, with a clear locked message",
    "Start schedule over with an explicit warning that scores will be lost",
    "Enter scores for both players in each match; draws allowed",
    "Correct or clear a previously entered score",
    "Match status badges (Waiting/Finished) and progress bar with finished/total/percent",
    "Filter matches by round, player, and status",
    "Live standings: played, won, drawn, lost, points for/against, difference, and points",
    "Tiebreaks: points, then score difference, then points scored, then alphabetical",
    "All data persists in localStorage across refresh; corrupted storage is recovered gracefully",
    "Responsive layout, semantic/accessible controls, empty and error states"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Scoring points for the standings are interpreted as goals/game points scored by a player (pointsFor) and conceded (pointsAgainst), with 'points' meaning the ranking points (win=3, draw=1). This matches the idea: 'points scored, points conceded, and their score difference' alongside 'A win is worth three points'.",
    "Player names are deduplicated case-insensitively and whitespace is trimmed so 'Alice' and 'alice' count as the same player.",
    "Scores must be non-negative integers; fractional or negative values are rejected with a clear error.",
    "The tournament is single-user and offline, so data is kept only in the browser's localStorage (no backend or accounts).",
    "Resetting the schedule returns the app to the setup phase, keeping the player list but clearing all matches and scores; players can then be edited again.",
    "Standings are shown only after the schedule is made; players with no completed matches still appear with zeroed stats."
  ],
